WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.875 --> 00:00:03.503
Planet Earth is so spectacular 

00:00:04.045 --> 00:00:06.923
it's easy to miss the smaller things in life.

00:00:10.969 --> 00:00:13.638
Strawberry dart frogs are tiny little frogs

00:00:13.638 --> 00:00:15.056
with a lot of personality.

00:00:15.056 --> 00:00:17.559
And they're only about the size of my thumbnail.

00:00:17.684 --> 00:00:18.601
We've brought this lens

00:00:18.601 --> 00:00:20.812
that's really meant for scientific purposes.

00:00:20.812 --> 00:00:22.480
And that allows us to get shots

00:00:22.480 --> 00:00:24.441
that we wouldn't have been able to otherwise.

00:00:24.774 --> 00:00:27.026
For days, we've been trying to get shots

00:00:27.026 --> 00:00:28.695
of two males wrestling.

00:00:28.695 --> 00:00:31.489
Because the males are territorial and quite competitive.

00:00:32.031 --> 00:00:34.451
And all of a sudden, these two males lock

00:00:34.451 --> 00:00:35.744
and they start going at it.

00:00:36.286 --> 00:00:37.162
And it got to the point

00:00:37.162 --> 00:00:38.955
where they actually jumped on the lens.

00:00:39.247 --> 00:00:40.623
And as a wildlife filmmaker

00:00:40.623 --> 00:00:43.710
you're always striving to film really natural behavior.

00:00:43.960 --> 00:00:45.336
So that was just amazing.

00:00:47.213 --> 00:00:49.549
I have quite a good amount of respect for goshawks.

00:00:49.549 --> 00:00:52.469
Like it is really, really hard to fly through this forest.

00:00:53.052 --> 00:00:54.637
They're not just trying to survive,

00:00:54.637 --> 00:00:56.431
and trying just not to hit a tree, they're hunting.

00:00:57.223 --> 00:00:58.767
Alright, let's go.

00:01:01.603 --> 00:01:04.189
These goshawks fly fifty miles an hour through here.

00:01:04.814 --> 00:01:05.732
Like, that must take

00:01:05.732 --> 00:01:08.067
incredible amounts of energy and focus.

00:01:08.401 --> 00:01:10.236
You don't just do that, easy.

00:01:13.782 --> 00:01:15.408
I don't think there's any other way

00:01:15.408 --> 00:01:16.743
to film the point of view of a goshawk.

00:01:16.743 --> 00:01:18.953
You need something that's very agile, nimble.

00:01:19.162 --> 00:01:20.330
Something that is forgiving.

00:01:20.330 --> 00:01:22.165
That's why we have these ducts on this drone.

00:01:22.165 --> 00:01:23.458
Because if you didn't have them,

00:01:23.458 --> 00:01:24.834
you hit anything, the propeller breaks

00:01:24.834 --> 00:01:26.211
and then the drone crashes.

00:01:35.345 --> 00:01:36.721
This is the golden-tailed gecko.

00:01:36.721 --> 00:01:37.931
Now I've been working with this gecko

00:01:37.931 --> 00:01:38.932
for the last three years,

00:01:38.932 --> 00:01:40.183
trying to film it in the wild.

00:01:41.893 --> 00:01:43.770
We've been using this motion control rig

00:01:43.770 --> 00:01:46.564
the way you'd use any other way of moving the camera,

00:01:46.564 --> 00:01:49.943
except just on a really, really tiny and precise scale.

00:01:50.860 --> 00:01:53.947
It's so close to these animals that are so small

00:01:53.947 --> 00:01:56.491
that there's no way that we could do them by hand

00:01:56.491 --> 00:01:58.535
and make them smooth and make them cinematic.

00:02:00.370 --> 00:02:03.248
I think it's actually a really powerful storytelling tool

00:02:03.248 --> 00:02:05.875
because you can be so specific with your shots.

00:02:05.875 --> 00:02:07.502
And you can literally take the story

00:02:07.502 --> 00:02:10.213
from one beat or one location, to the next.

00:02:10.713 --> 00:02:12.340
-Can we replay that little bit?
-Yeah.

00:02:15.802 --> 00:02:17.720
-Oh, yes!
-Yes!

00:02:18.680 --> 00:02:21.182
See the world from a new perspective.

00:02:22.016 --> 00:02:22.934
Tiny World.

